abstract: "GLPlot is a high-performance, GPU-accelerated plotting library for Python that provides a Matplotlib-compatible API with OpenGL/GLFW backend support. It efficiently handles millions of geometric primitives through instanced rendering and advanced density visualization techniques, enabling interactive scientific visualization at scale."
